      "explanation": "<p>Option (A) : Correct. The complex [Co(en)(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>(H<sub>2</sub>O)]<sup>3+</sup> has two following isomers:</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 53 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kywp3axv/f70ef7a4-c0a1-40a3-b43a-d713b8eeffb7/6416c730-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3axw.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n<p>Option (B) : Correct. When bidentate 'en' is replaced by two cyanide ligands complex [Co(CN)<sub>2</sub>(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>(H<sub>2</sub>O)]<sup>+</sup> will have three following isomers:</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2018 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 53 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kywp3tn0/fdd95d4e-3427-4021-b888-fdc13b86e5af/728870c0-7f48-11ec-9a1e-9f87431102fd/file-1kywp3tn1.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"> </p>\n<p>Option (C) : Incorrect. Incomplex [Co(en)(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>(H<sub>2</sub>O)]<sup>3+</sup>, Co is in + 3 oxidation, that is, [Ar]d<sup>6</sup>. In the presence given ligands the complex will have low spin, hence, diamagnetic.</p>\n<p>Option (D) : Correct. In complex [Co(en)(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>4</sub>]<sup>3+</sup> there is larger gap between t<sub>2g</sub> and e<sub>g</sub> than in complex [Co(en)(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>(H<sub>2</sub>O)]<sup>3+</sup>. Hence [Co(en)(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>(H<sub>2</sub>O)]<sup>3+</sup> will absorb light at longer wavelength as compared to [Co(en)(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>4</sub>]<sup>3+</sup>.</p>"
    }
  ]
